note SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT
note COURIER lane: Allen's courier to the Spark relay over UDP 47033, the Omega
note build's x86/courier_udp_x86.c. application.om (appinit, appask, apppoll,
note appsent, appreceive) already speaks the courier wire; this module binds its
note datagrams to net.om's netudpsend/Chrx hooks and the typed line to appask.
note Needs base, runtime, code, courier, scheduler, memory, intent, reply,
note context, application (gate.sh core list) and net.om before it in the unit.
note Ch: 0 initialized, 1 last event, 2 datagrams out, 3 datagrams in,
note 4 refused sends, 5 answers taken, 6 run id, 7 dropped-at-receive seen.
note Chevent after chstep: 0 nothing, 1 answer visible in Chsay, 2 asked AGAIN,
note 3 gave up, 4 refused, 5 slow notice, 6 silence (application.om A2).
global Ch ulong 8
global Chsay uchar 320
global Chsayn ulong 1
global Chevent ulong 1
note Run id like the C kernel: the clock at start mixed with the MAC, never 0.
fn chrun now ulong to ulong
run = now
for i ulong 6
run = xor run shl ulong get Nmac i mul 8 add i 2
end
if eq run 0
run = 1
end
ret run
end
note Refused (false, nothing touched) while application.om is still active.
fn chinit now ulong run ulong to bool
if eq run 0
run = chrun now
end
if not appinit run now
ret false
end
for i ulong 8
put Ch i 0
end
put Chsayn 0 0
put Chevent 0 0
put Chrxn 0 0
put Chdrop 0 0
put Ch 0 1
put Ch 6 run
ret true
end
note The typed request is platform.om's Dprm[0..Dprmn); appask copies and
note validates it (1..159 printable bytes). Dprmn is left for the caller.
fn chask now ulong to bool
if eq get Ch 0 0
ret false
end
n = get Dprmn 0
if gt n len Dprm
ret false
end
for i ulong n
put In i get Dprm i
end
put Inlen 0 n
ret appask now
end
fn chbusy to bool
if eq get Ch 0 0
ret false
end
ret or ne get R 1 0 ne get A 1 0
end
fn chcancel to void
if eq get Ch 0 0
ret
end
appcancel
put Chevent 0 0
end
fn chsay to void
n = get R 8
if gt n len Chsay
n = len Chsay
end
for i ulong n
put Chsay i get Answer i
end
put Chsayn 0 n
put Ch 5 add get Ch 5 1
end
fn chevent to void
e = get A 2
if eq e 0
ret
end
put Chevent 0 e
put Ch 1 e
if eq e 1
chsay
end
end
fn chtake now ulong to void
n = get Chrxn 0
put Chrxn 0 0
put Ch 3 add get Ch 3 1
put Ch 7 get Chdrop 0
for i ulong n
put In i get Chrx i
end
put Inlen 0 n
if appreceive now
chevent
end
end
fn chsend now ulong to void
n = get Outlen 0
ok = false
if and ne n 0 le n len Chtx
for i ulong n
put Chtx i get Outb i
end
ok = netudpsend n
end
if ok
put Ch 2 add get Ch 2 1
else
put Ch 4 add get Ch 4 1
end
ok = appsent now ok
end
note One step of the courier, like the C pump: take the datagram waiting in
note Chrx, then let the scheduler offer HELLO/JOB/GOT and send it. up is the
note firmware's network-up flag (Es 6). Chevent reports this step's event.
fn chstep now ulong up bool to void
put Chevent 0 0
if eq get Ch 0 0
ret
end
if ne get Chrxn 0 0
chtake now
end
off = apppoll now up
chevent
if off
chsend now
end
end
